<title>AUSTRIA: Venezuela does not accept over-producing - Iran.</title>
<headline>Venezuela does not accept over-producing - Iran.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iranian oil minister Gholamreza Aghazadeh said after a meeting with Venezuelan oil minister Erwin Jose Arrieta that the latter did not accept his country was producing over its OPEC quota.</p>
<p>&quot;He didn't accept even one barrel of over-production,&quot; Aghazadeh said, adding that he had had a very good meeting with Arrieta.  </p>
<p>Venezuela's OPEC quota stands at 2.359 million barrels per day (bpd) but according to a Reuter survey it pumped 3.15 million bpd in October.</p>
<p>Bilateral talks between ministers continued on Wednesday ahead of the full session scheduled for 1400 gmt.</p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom +431 713 2034</p>
</text>
